# Citation metadata for Quantum Anchor.
#
# BEFORE PUBLISHING — two things here must be decided by a human, not by the
# tooling:
#
# 1. THE AUTHOR LIST. The entry below is the named author, confirmed by the
#    project owner. A Zenodo DOI is permanent and public, and it cannot be
#    quietly reassigned later — being named on it is a public, citable
#    attribution, so anyone added later must agree to be named.
#
# 2. THE DOI. Zenodo mints it on the first upload. Put the CONCEPT DOI here (the
#    one covering all versions), not the version DOI: the concept DOI always
#    resolves to the latest release. No DOI is listed below yet, because
#    inventing a placeholder identifier risks it being copied into a real
#    citation. Add it after the first successful Zenodo upload.
#
# The ORCID below is an all-zero placeholder, which is the conventional
# "no ORCID" sentinel. Replace it with a real one, or delete the field — do
# not leave a fabricated identifier in place.
#
# The affiliation is now CONSISTENT across all four files: this file,
# .zenodo.json, docs/HOPE-WP-2026-V1.2.md and arxiv/quantum_anchor_v1.2.tex all
# say "Hope Ecosystem". (This note previously reported an inconsistency between
# "Independent" and "Hope Ecosystem"; that was resolved on 2026-10-08 by
# changing this file and .zenodo.json, and the note was left stale until then.)
# An affiliation is an employment claim and a Zenodo DOI is permanent and
# public — if it ever changes again, update all four files together.
#
# The repository URL is the intended public location. Confirm it resolves
# before tagging a release — the sdist check and the Zenodo record depend on it.
#
# The abstract deliberately states the negative results. If you shorten it to a
# positive summary, it will misrepresent the work.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantum Anchor Protocol: Frequency-Domain Wave-Packet Encoding with Hardware-Validated Quantum Bridge"
abstract: >-
  Quantum Anchor Protocol encodes a frequency-domain wave packet into quantum
  interference circuits. This release adds a hardware-validated quantum bridge:
  the encoding was measured on a real 156-qubit superconducting QPU (IBM
  ibm_marrakesh, 2000 shots per run, 2026-10-06), reaching 99.3% Bell balance
  on two qubits, 98.8% on a reproducibility run, and an ideal three-qubit GHZ
  distribution. The decoding formulas' assumption P(q0=1)=sin^2(theta/2) is
  therefore measurement-verified rather than assumed.

  Tesseract-V3 5-phase interferometric sweep on IQM Garnet (20Q, Starter tier):
  5 phases, 1024 shots each (5120 total). Wilson 95% CIs: [0.74, 2.16],
  [0.10, 0.86], [0.05, 0.71], [0.82, 2.28], [0.10, 0.86] (%). Aggregate:
  0.68% [0.45%, 1.01%]. Chi2 vs cos(8φ): 0.83 (df=4). Chi2 vs flat: 1.98 (df=4).
  Cos(8φ) fit: offset=0.68%, amplitude=0.51% (theory: 1.56%, 3x smaller), R²=0.48.
  Evidence grade: C (Noise-dominated — NO phase discrimination, both models within χ² envelope, no decisive rejection). All 5 phase audits saved 2026-10-11.
  Pulse-level anchor drive blocked by IQM Starter tier (pulse access denied).

  Classical and hardware proofs are reported as strictly separate evidence
  levels. Negative results reported honestly.
